{"kind":"artifact","text":"The layer contract drops a claim that was false and states only the categories exercised. Exact clean pushed head 937389e1c7498095073395fb094819049700ad4c on request/repo-remote-link; tree ce30bc6b, checkout clean, origin matching. Under planner's repair child 40862781 and my promise a5d65234.\n\nTHE FALSE CLAIM IS GONE. The page said a repository owned by another user is refused outright. That is not true under sudo, where Git widens owner-trust from an inherited SUDO_UID — codex found it and I did not test it, because doing so needs root and I was not going to run an execution vector as root to confirm something I already accepted.\n\nWHAT IT SAYS INSTEAD. Only what was exercised: that two ownership allowances Git would otherwise take from the environment do not reach these commands — safe.directory, honoured now only from the pinned scopes, and the sudo widening via SUDO_UID — and the cost, that running these reads under sudo refuses reads that used to succeed.\n\nTHE MECHANISM PARAGRAPH now describes the allowlist rather than a denied set, names the four escapes that made a blocklist untenable, and records the os.DevNull choice and PATH's honest status. The citation guard's paragraph stays a property statement per planner's ruling, with its wording widened from 'no list of variable names is load-bearing' to 'no enumeration of variables, admitted or denied' — because an allowlist is still an enumeration, and the property has to survive that too.\n\nTHE GITSTORE SHARING NOTE is here rather than implemented, per planner's guidance: the same mechanism belongs in internal/gitstore, and that is a separate request gated on a ruling from hugh.\n\nONE THING I KNOW IS INCOMPLETE. This page's rests_on front matter does not name the internal/app artifact for this head, so it cannot flare when that behaviour moves. It cannot: the artifact id does not exist until after the commit that would have to contain it. The docset gate is green here and this is the same shape every head on this lane has had, but it is a real gap rather than an oversight, and it belongs in a row about anchoring rather than in silence.\n\nGATES, run by me at this exact head from a run I watched exit. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0: 34 ok and 1 with no test files, zero failures and zero cached. npm test 131 pass, 0 fail. gofmt empty; build, vet, GOOS=windows build of internal/app, and diff-check all exit 0; make ui leaves git status empty; make ui-check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"937389e1c7498095073395fb094819049700ad4c","path":"docs/reference/architecture.md"}}